note Translated from CPython Lib/shlex.py shlex.sourcehook (lines 277 to 285).
note Hook called on a filename to be sourced.

choice InputSource
    note WORKAROUND: Python tests `isinstance(self.infile, str)`; infile may be a file name or None (or another object), so a choice stands in for the dynamic type test
    Named with path as a Path
    Unnamed

type Shlex
    field infile as an InputSource
    note ... the other shlex fields

note WORKAROUND: Python returns the tuple (newfile, open(newfile, "r")); the doc has no tuple, so a named record is declared
type SourcedFile
    field name as a Path
    field stream as a TextFile

to is_absolute path
    given path is Text
    produces a Bool

to directory_of path
    given path is a Path
    produces a Path

to join base with name
    given base is a Path
    given name is Text
    produces Text

note GAP: objects, methods and self - sourcehook is a method that subclasses override to change sourcing; the doc has no methods, no self and no overriding, so it is written as a plain operation taking the lexer
to sourcehook newfile for lexer using files
    given newfile is Text
    given lexer is a Shlex
    given files is a FileSystem
    produces a SourcedFile
    fails with FileError
    uses files

    var name starts at newfile
    note UNCLEAR: Python indexes newfile[0], which raises IndexError on an empty string; the doc has no character type and no rule for an out-of-range index, so `first character of` is a guess
    note GAP: characters and slicing - `newfile[0] == '"'` and `newfile[1:-1]` need a character literal and a slice with a negative end; the doc has neither
    if first character of name is "\""
        set name to characters 1 until (length of name - 1) of name
    note This implements cpp-like semantics for relative-path inclusion.
    choose infile of lexer
        when Named with path
            if not is_absolute name
                set name to join (directory_of path) with name
        when Unnamed
            note nothing to adjust: the lexer was not reading from a named file
            note UNCLEAR: the doc has no "do nothing" statement and does not say whether a when branch holding only a note is allowed
    note GAP: an operation that returns an open file inside a record - the caller owns the stream and must close it; hold only covers scoped use, and the doc does not show a produces line that hands a linear resource to the caller
    let stream be try open name for reading using files
    note UNCLEAR: the doc has no general form for building a record; this follows `an Order from cart and receipt with status Paid` in example 29
    give back a SourcedFile with name name and stream stream
